  "conclusion": "The four kernel properties are NOT trivially satisfiable. While 2-byte vocabulary patterns appear in any sequence (composition-dependent), structure-dependent patterns (>=4 bytes) are 10421x more frequent in real proteins, consistent with the previously established 22x (4-byte) and 136x (5-byte) shuffled genome ratios. Programs and dispatch networks built from structure-dependent words collapse in random sequences. The framework rejects non-biological input."
